GAIA//GENESIS licensing scope

GAIA-authored application code is licensed under GNU GPL version 3, with the
additional permission below. See COPYING for the complete GPL-3.0 text.

Additional permission under GNU GPL version 3 section 7:
For GAIA-authored host application code only, you may link or combine that code
with GSAP under the Standard GSAP License and convey the resulting application.
GSAP remains subject to its own license. This permission does not apply to any
third-party code, including Julien Sulpis's shaders, or to the standalone Atlas
renderer program (src/atlas/renderer.worker.ts).

The Atlas renderer is a separate GPL-3.0-only Web Worker program, built into its
own bundle. It contains the GPL shaders, uses WebGL2/OffscreenCanvas directly,
imports no GSAP/Three.js/GAIA renderer, and exchanges serialized commands with
the host. The complete corresponding source, build scripts and pinned package
lock are distributed in this public repository. No GSAP exception is asserted
for the upstream shaders. src/vendor/jsulpis/LICENSE is their original license.

Previously imported MIT/BSD/Zlib sources, fonts and all texture assets retain
their respective licenses and attribution; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and
docs/ATLAS_SOURCE.md. This file does not relicense third-party works.
